  "summary": "Fixes Include-What-You-Use (IWYU) warnings in fuzz test targets under `src/test/fuzz` and configures CI to treat them as errors. Introduces a linter to ensure header contents stay enclosed within include guards, extracts `NodeId` into a dedicated `node/node_id.h` header to avoid ambiguous duplicate declarations, and adjusts transitive includes in `net` and `node/eviction`.",
  "problem": "Missing explicit `#include` directives in fuzz targets allow transitive header dependencies to proliferate unchecked, complicating static analysis and header refactoring. Ambiguous duplicate declarations (such as `NodeId`) also prevent IWYU tooling from identifying canonical source headers.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'This PR continues the ongoing effort to enforce IWYU warnings.'",
    "Commit 86296b1bf6: 'Two identical declarations of `NodeId` make it ambiguous for static tools such as IWYU which header should provide the symbol. Move the declaration into a header of its own.'"
  ],
